My question is, why do you need commas in those places? Commas only 
separate vowels that you don't want to run into a dipthong (".ie" versus 
".i,e" for example). But I guess a semicolon would work. Maybe a backtick 
(`) if you don't like that extra dot floating around. I haven't seen any 
official alternatives, though.

